<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cardamine-hirsuta-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength on Cardamine hirsuta at 154 µm (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 80.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Holocene (0 Ma) detail-scale Schnakenberg model with slot coefficients a=0.10, b=0.90, D_u=0.04, D_v=0.42. Classical lambda_c is pinned at 154.1 µm (k_c^2 = 185/21). Self-test dispersion Pearson r = 0.9999, RMSE = 0.00156, equal-diffusion sigma_max = -0.102, and a monotonic rise in selected wavelength from 164 µm to 217 µm as D_v/D_u goes from 10.5 to 40. Nonlinear spacing on two seeds is 173.4 µm, 12% longer than the classical law. The 12-frame 720x540 GIF scores CV similarity 96.0 against the public-domain plant. Pass 1 does not yet treat those sidecar measurements as the scored record. Overall 80.2/100 (faithfulness 77.6, reproducibility 86.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 78, Morphometric validation 74, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-cardamine-hirsuta-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 344427 B, 1440×860 px, artifact_sha256 42f28ae17a71284a0b1d2844190e61edcef85400790a837f1209e520802e70ec (sha256 42f28ae17a71284a0b1d2844190e61edcef85400790a837f1209e520802e70ec), spec_fingerprint 619c6e2e8c89814d4927f6c66381065778340adfaf1d52680367bc6b98ea29d7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 619c6e2e8c89814d4927f6c66381065778340adfaf1d52680367bc6b98ea29d7; artifact_sha256: 42f28ae17a71284a0b1d2844190e61edcef85400790a837f1209e520802e70ec; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=03de545ad27ccbf4..., datasets/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0/cardamine_hirsuta_specimen.jpg=1c268fecb3660b31..., datasets/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=c696a1319c853366..., datasets/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=bfcb6bdfc46bcf19..., datasets/cardamine_hirsuta_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=79d1ae5d5b27c95e...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite critical wavenumber from reaction and diffusion. | Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v. | Kierzkowski et al. (2019) and Vlad et al. (2014) describe Cardamine hirsuta leaflet growth and the RCO domain-size difference from Arabidopsis. | Fuster-Pons et al. (2024) describe a lateral-inhibition trichome pattern in Cardamine.; reconstructed_in_script: Neumann Schnakenberg integration, the dispersion fit, the diffusivity sweep, and the equal-diffusion ablation. | Physical calibration that sets the classical wavelength equal to 154.1 µm. | Pigment-ocellus readout of activator u inside the photographed leaf mask.; transfer_boundary: 154.1 µm is the slot scale assigned to the classical wavenumber, not a length quoted from the Cardamine papers. | Trichome spacing is a related epidermal periodicity, not the pigment field drawn here.; does_not_claim: That the whole-plant photograph resolves 154 µm ocelli. | That a named fossil chronospecies precedes or follows this Holocene terminal (series 1/1, age 0 Ma). | That the nonlinear spacing of 173.4 µm falsifies or confirms a published Cardamine measurement.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/specimen-match, pressure P=0.5]: A second assessor has not scored this loop.",
        "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=3.0]: Fingerprint ablation, segmentation, Pearson r, RMSE, and KS.",
        "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=2.5]: Fingerprint the D_v sweep in the measurement sidecar.",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Score the five-point D_v sweep monotonicity from the measurement sidecar, not only from the figure.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Score the equal-diffusion ablation (sigma_max < 0 and a falling field standard deviation) as a negative control.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Record specimen segmentation (foreground fraction, aspect, circularity, coherency) with references that are not copies of the measured values.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Record dispersion Pearson r, RMSE, and the specimen-versus-render orientation KS statistic.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Independent second assessor. This Pass 1 score is a single-agent reading.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.02e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

